{"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"content","content":[{"text":"Overview","level":2,"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Corpus (in progress — 2 of 69)","level":2,"anchor":"Corpus-in-progress-2-of-69","type":"heading"},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The translated corpus is the gallery and the training set. Each entry is a","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"verified SwiftUI translation of an Origami pattern.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"text":"Interaction","level":3,"anchor":"Interaction","type":"heading"},{"type":"unorderedList","items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:Interaction_Touch"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_Drag","type":"reference"}]}]}]}]}],"variants":[{"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}],"paths":["\/documentation\/swami"]}],"schemaVersion":{"major":0,"patch":0,"minor":3},"topicSections":[{"title":"Reference